DTSTART:20150215T190000Z
DTEND:20150215T220000Z
DTSTAMP:20260512T040225Z
UID:oeofn4htvfm6agjc473o7ig7os@google.com
CREATED:20150205T213253Z
DESCRIPTION:For details\, link here: https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/raspberry-
 pi-workshop-getting-started-with-physical-computing-tickets-15644682667\n\n
 Getting started with Raspberry Pi physical computing workshop.All are welco
 me. We will hsow you how to start working with Rasberry Pi and get it to in
 teract with the physical world. This will include setting up the Pi\, conne
 cting some electronic components to it and doing a "Hello World" project.\n
 Please bring a laptop and a Pi if you have one\, we will have a number of t
 hem provided\, but probably not enough for everyone.You can buy one at Crea
 tron at 255 College Street or online at http://canada.newark.com . The new 
 version of Pi just came out\, but is still on backorder at Newark(element14
 )\, so it will be a dilemma for you - get an "older" B+ or wait for new Rpi
 2 :)\nIf you have any ideas for a project\, bring it along with any compone
 nts you might need and we will help you get statrted with that!\nFinding Ha
 cklab: We’re at Queen and Dufferin\, NW corner\, buzz unit #12.\nA PWCY (pa
 y what you can) donation of $10 is suggested. Nobody turned away for lack o
 f funds.
LAST-MODIFIED:20150205T213330Z
LOCATION:1266 Queen St. West Toronto\, ON M6K 1L3 - 
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Raspberry Pi Workshop: Getting Started with Physical Computing
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:HackLab.TO
DTSTART:20151130T230000Z
DTEND:20151201T020000Z
DTSTAMP:20260512T040225Z
UID:437550EB-5F48-4342-89DA-8CAA867991CC
CREATED:20151106T220608Z
DESCRIPTION:A Stitch 'n Bitch is generally just a gathering of people who a
 re into fabric-hacking and making\, where everyone can gather around\, show
  off their gear and techniques\, and generally just talk about things. \n\n
 Anyone can attend! Bring in some clothing you want to modify and you can do
  it on the serger or sewing machines\, or your knitting/sewing materials\, 
 or your spinning wheel\, or anything else you think might be appropriate. C
 ome learn to knit or crochet! Or just show up and chat and watch others do 
 their thing.
LAST-MODIFIED:20151130T223005Z
LOCATION:HackLab Classroom
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Fibre Hacking Night
TRANSP:OPAQUE
