DTSTART:20180302T003000Z
DTEND:20180302T023000Z
DTSTAMP:20260512T040225Z
UID:22C795D0-4C1F-4540-9FD8-E7834BC070F0
CREATED:20180103T035356Z
DESCRIPTION:Eventbrite: https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/arduino-for-beginners-t
 ickets-42790706154\nFacebook Event: https://www.facebook.com/events/1490142
 35760545/\n\nArduino Beginners Workshop [parts extra]. For total beginners.
  All are welcome. A-Train and Zach will show you how to get started with Ar
 duino\, the super-friendly microcontroller platform that even artists love.
  We’ll cover getting the software installed and going\, hooking up the Ardu
 ino\, and a little bit of basic programming\, via explanation of the Exampl
 es. You too can cut and paste your way to a working project!\n***If you can
 't bring your own Arduino (any kind will do) and any cables required to att
 ach it to your laptop (typically an A to B USB cable)\, we'll be selling ki
 ts included with your Eventbrite purchase. You'll also need a laptop on whi
 ch you can install software. You can purchase an Arduino at Creatron at  34
 9 College St\, Toronto\, ON M5T 1S5 (or online\, of course). The Arduino Un
 o is the recommended board for beginners\, but any arduino will do if you h
 ave a more specialized project in mind.***\nFinding Hacklab: We're at Queen
  and Dufferin\, NW corner\, buzz unit #12.
LAST-MODIFIED:20180302T003254Z
LOCATION:Hacklab\, 1266 Queen Street West #12\, Toronto\, ON\, Canada
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Arduino Beginners Workshop with ATrain and Zach
TRANSP:OPAQUE
