BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:HackLab.TO
DTSTART:20140424T230000Z
DTEND:20140425T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260512T040225Z
UID:7aqkfj7fgov3tinqmuktcrf6g0@google.com
CREATED:20140331T182320Z
DESCRIPTION:Hey\, Sen and I had a conversation about all the stuff being st
 ored at hacklab.  We'd like to get people to take some of it home.  Much of
  it is theoretically useful\, but in practice not actually used.  The GOAL 
 is to get a lot of stuff out of hacklab\, so that we can reduce clutter and
  make the space more usable.  Also\, less stuff means less stuff to move wh
 en that happens.\n\nSo\, I'm scheduling a day where we're going to look at 
 everything in the lab\, and make a lot of decisions about what stays and wh
 at goes.  I want to look at EVERYTHING in the lab\, all the nooks and crann
 ies\, all the stuff on the shelves\, etc.  The main rule is\, if only ONE p
 erson wants it at the lab\, they have to take it home themselves.  Things c
 an stay only if two or more members want it here.  Things which nobody supp
 orts will probably go to ewaste.\n\nI'm calling it "lab take-home day"\, an
 d it will be THURSDAY APRIL 24th\, 7-9pm.  There will be FREE PIZZA. \n\nCo
 me one come all\, help us make hacklab less cluttered.\n\nWe're gonna do th
 e whole lab\, but here's some areas we're going to focus on:\n - the kitche
 n (all cupboards & counters)\n - the bookshelf by the blackboard\n - the ol
 d tower of fabrication\n - the milk crates\n - the blue table area by the c
 ouch\n - the stuff on the floor in the closet\n - the bikeshed\n - the two 
 window ledges\n\nEric\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20140331T182344Z
LOCATION:hacklab.TO\, 170A Baldwin Street\, Toronto
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:lab take-home day
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
