BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:HackLab.TO
DTSTART:20110222T000000Z
DTEND:20110222T020000Z
DTSTAMP:20260512T040225Z
UID:bqsmglc09lj60ro5pdhnq9mm8g@google.com
CREATED:20110210T225218Z
DESCRIPTION:RSVP here (limit 10 people\, $20 each):\nhttp://www.eventbrite.
 com/event/1310360323\nhttp://hacklab.to/archives/arduino-workshop-ii/\n\nHa
 cklab will be hosting a follow-up to the previous Arduino workshop\, since 
 it was so popular. I’ve scheduled it for Monday Feb 21st at 7pm\, which is 
 two weeks from tomorrow.\n\nThis workshop will be a little more advanced th
 an the last one\, and there will be a materials fee\, so that we can have a
  little more to work with than some surplus LEDs\, and you’ll get to take s
 tuff home with you. I’m not sure exactly what that cost will be (gotta go t
 o Creatron and see how much the stuff I am thinking of will cost)\, but we’
 ll be learning some bread boarding skills (laying out a more complicated ci
 rcuit)\, and writing a moderate sized program. I expect the class to take a
 bout 2 hours total. It will be helpful if you’ve already done at least the 
 Blink tutorial (as we did the last time)\, but total beginners are welcome 
 as always. Hacklab-membership not required\, but RSVP will be – attendance 
 will be capped so that I know how many kits of stuff to buy\, and we have r
 oom to work. Watch this blog for RSVP link to follow sometime in the next w
 eek.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20221122T084108Z
LOCATION:Hacklab.to\, 170A Baldwin Street\, Toronto\, Canada
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Hacklab: Arduino Tutorial II
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
