UID:3m4b0nlie7vo8oode2f6hbcjd8@google.com
CREATED:20141201T175223Z
DESCRIPTION:http://wintersoldering1.eventbrite.ca\n\nWant to learn how to s
 older?  Missed your chance at the Toronto Mini Maker Faire?  Hacklab is off
 ering a learn how to solder class for total beginners\, using the snowbot k
 it from the faire!  You'll learn the process of soldering\, which is how el
 ectronic components get attached to printed circuit boards (PCBs) to make f
 unctional circuits.  The process involves a (hot) soldering iron and solder
 \, a metal with a very low melting point.\n\nThe kit is snowbot: a 3 LED (l
 ight emitting diode\, they are tiny high-efficiency high-brightness lights)
  kit which uses a CR2032 coin-cell battery.  You can choose your LEDs from 
 amongst a vast assortment of colors and styles\, plus you can customize you
 r snowbot with a scarf and posable arms.  Makes a great Christmas tree orna
 ment!\n\nTickets on eventbrite are free (we're using them to control arriva
 l times)\, but there is a pay-what-you-want minimum $3 cost for each snowbo
 t kit you will pay at the event\, so bring some coins or small bills.  This
  covers our materials cost and any additional you donate helps support hack
 lab\, a technology community space in Parkdale.  We share resources\, tools
  and expertise so that people can do fun things with tech.
LAST-MODIFIED:20141216T020000Z
LOCATION:Hacklab.TO\, 1266 Queen Street West #12\, Toronto
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:winter soldering workshop at hacklab
TRANSP:OPAQUE
