UID:fle77pek9bkutu57do71gjovjc@google.com
CREATED:20130704T151519Z
DESCRIPTION:http://hacklab-arduino.eventbrite.com/\n\nArduino Beginners Wor
 kshop. For total beginners. All are welcome. Eric will show you how to get 
 started with Arduino\, the super-friendly microcontroller platform that eve
 n artists love. We’ll cover getting the software installed and going\, hook
 ing up the Arduino\, and a little bit of basic programming\, via explanatio
 n of the Examples. You too can cut and paste your way to a working project!
  You’ll need to bring your own Arduino (any kind will do) and a laptop on w
 hich you can install software. Also please bring any cables required to att
 ach your Arduino to your laptop – typically this means an A to B USB cable.
  If you do not have an Arduino\, you can purchase one at Creatron\, only a 
 few blocks away from Hacklab at 255 College Street.
LAST-MODIFIED:20221122T084246Z
LOCATION:Hacklab.to\, 170A Baldwin Street\, Toronto\, Canada
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Arduino Total Beginners Workshop at Hacklab.to
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:HackLab.TO
DTSTART:20161126T190000Z
DTEND:20161126T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260512T040225Z
UID:oefohds3q4d7momu85lc6f1pb0@google.com
CREATED:20161113T212538Z
DESCRIPTION:Lately I've been doing a lot of reading and thinking on the sub
 ject of "creative career design"\, basically\, leading life in a non-tradit
 ional way\, trying to have it your way.  I'm ready for a big change in my l
 ife\, but I don't know what I'd like to do next\, or how to even judge poss
 ibilities in an effective way.  Ideally what I'd like to do is figure out h
 ow to make a living while doing something that I enjoy\, that has a huge po
 sitive impact on the world.  Obviously that's a lot to ask\; I feel like to
  stand any chance at it\, I will need to get extremely creative and do a lo
 t of thinking outside the box\, testing of unusual ideas\, getting feedback
  from tons of people\, etc.\n\nI'm sure I'm not alone in wanting this kind 
 of change\, or a career with those properties.  If you're interested in tal
 king about this kind of thing\, please join me at hacklab Saturday Nov 26th
 \, 2-4pm for an invigorating group discussion in the classroom.  I'll be br
 inging a few conversation starting questions and my own story.\n\nEric 
LAST-MODIFIED:20161113T213006Z
LOCATION:Hacklab\, 1266 Queen St W\, Toronto\, ON M6K 1L3\, Canada
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Creative Career Design salon
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
