DTSTART:20160919T230000Z
DTEND:20160920T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260512T040225Z
UID:tggopmhtr75mf12cr1d5pun3t8@google.com
CREATED:20160721T181511Z
DESCRIPTION:http://www.meetup.com/GTA-Robotics/events/232939501/?rv=co1\n\n
 Let's talk about Personal/Service/Mobility robots including AI based like E
 cho\, or non-mobile like Jibo\, and how to get started in DIY robotics to b
 uild your own personal assistant.\n\nThis time we will meet in downtown Tor
 onto at Hacklab.TO\, a very nice makerspace with lots of opportunities for 
 DIY robotics.\n\nWith this occasion I would like to bring up again the role
  of makerspaces for robotics education and DIY\, and discuss how to get kid
 s/adults inspired through activities organized there.\n\nIf you'll like to 
 do a presentation please send me the title and a short description\, and I'
 ll add it to the agenda.\n\nSo far we have two presentations:\n\n- X-Drive 
 - Manual to Power Wheel Chair Conversion Kit - Alex Shortt \nRobot descript
 ion: \nOur project solution is a smart phone controlled power conversion ki
 t that fits the majority of manual wheelchairs. \nThe kit is be easily remo
 vable\, has a simple initial setup and meets the minimum speed of a walking
  pace. By being app-controlled\, the system does away with the conventional
  joystick. This adds convenience to the user as they can use their own mobi
 le device or tablet as well as complexity to the project. The product will 
 also not affect the mobility of the manual wheelchair by using a compact de
 sign.\n\n- SPARK (STEMCA Personal Assistant Robot Kit) - Marius Slavescu \n
 An affordable and easy to use/program DIY kit for building telepresence\, h
 ome smart monitoring and control\, companion robots for kids/seniors\, buil
 t on top of STEMCA Inventor platform - https://hackaday.io/project/7138-ste
 mca-inventor-stem-education-and-diy-amplified\n\nX-Drive is a very interest
 ing DIY robotics project in the mobility space that won first place in the 
 robotics competition at Innovation Nation Conference 2016: \nhttp://innovat
 ion-nation.ca/archives-2/2016-competition-winnersRobot\n\nYou can find out 
 more and vote for the project here: \nhttp://contest.techbriefs.com/2016/en
 tries/consumer-products/7042\n\nAs always please bring your projects for sh
 ow and tell\, the more projects we see live and discuss about the more insp
 ired we get.\n\nWe will also have a retrospective of most interesting and i
 nspiring robotics/making events of the month\, from GTA.\n\nThank you Eric 
 for offering us the space for this meeting.
LAST-MODIFIED:20160919T223109Z
LOCATION:Hacklab\, 1266 Queen St W\, Toronto\, ON M6K 1L3\, Canada
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:GTA Robotics Meeting details TBD
TRANSP:OPAQUE
