DESCRIPTION:Despite the great success of lab take-home day\, some things di
 d not get looked at\, due to time constraints.  In particular\, here's a qu
 ick list of stuff we still need to go over:\n\n1) the book collection.  I t
 hink without too much trouble we could reduce it to two full shelves instea
 d of three partial ones.\n2) the closet - mostly just the acrylic/laser mat
 erial collection\, it's out of control.\n3) the bikeshed - there is a lot o
 f stuff we should just pitch\, probably\, and hopefully we can get things l
 ike the ladder into there once we're done\n4) the lathe area\n\nTo that end
 \, I'm scheduling a lab "spring cleaning" day\, MONDAY MAY 12th\, 7-9pm.  A
 s before\, free pizza for all who come to help! Let's clean up all these ar
 eas and otherwise make the lab super neat and awesome.\n\nEric\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20140429T183130Z
LOCATION:hacklab.to\, 170A Baldwin Street\, Toronto
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:hacklab spring cleaning
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
