CREATED:20110824T192457Z
DESCRIPTION:We’ve received some queries for further details on the Arduino 
 Workshop. So here’s some more info for those of you thinking of coming:\n\n
 Arduino Total Beginners Workshop\nMonday Sept 12th 2011\, 7pm-9pm\nYou’ll n
 eed to bring your own Arduino (any kind will do) and a laptop on which you 
 can install software. Also please bring any cables required to attach your 
 Arduino to your laptop – typically this means an A to B USB cable. If you d
 o not have an Arduino\, you can purchase one at Creatron\, only a few block
 s away from hacklab at 255 College Street.\n\nAs before\, all are welcome\,
  no RSVP required. Eric will show you how to get started with Arduino\, the
  super-friendly microcontroller platform that even artists love. We’ll cove
 r getting the software installed and going\, hooking up the Arduino\, and a
  little bit of basic programming\, via explanation of the Examples. You too
  can cut and paste your way to a working project!
LAST-MODIFIED:20221122T083659Z
LOCATION:Hacklab.to\, 170A Baldwin Street
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Hacklab Arduino Beginners Workshop
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
