DESCRIPTION:http://www.ontariosciencecentre.ca/Calendar/112/\n\nI got to se
 e this exhibit shortly after it opened\, a few months ago\, and it's *incre
 dible*.  Hundreds of old video games\, in a playable state\, including arca
 de machines\, old consoles\, handheld games\, etc.etc.\n\nI propose a hackl
 ab field trip to visit this thing and game ourselves into happy bliss.  Hou
 rs at the Ontario Science Center are 10am to 5pm on Weekends.  Admission fo
 r Adults is $22. \n\nHow about Saturday July 13th\, 10am-5pm as the Hacklab
  Vintage Gaming Day?  Let me know if there is some terrible reason it shoul
 dn't be on that day.  We'd meet there\, so show anytime you like\, but real
 ly for $22 you should get there as early as you can to get your money's wor
 th :-)\n\nHere's some samples from what they have:\n\nVirtusphere — a 10-fo
 ot hollow sphere that allows a user to enter and run freely while wearing a
  wireless\, head-mounted display\nLemmings - Commodore Amiga\nTetris - Nint
 endo Gameboy\nMario Kart 64 - Nintendo 64 \nSuper Breakout - Atari 2600\nLe
 gend of Zelda - Nintendo NES (US)\nGolden Eye 007 - Nintendo Wii\nDonkey Ko
 ng - Arcade\nPac-Man - Arcade\n\nAnd tons and tons more.\n\nEric\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20221122T083616Z
LOCATION:Ontario Science Center\, 770 Don Mills Road\, Toronto
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Hacklab Vintage Gaming Day - Ontario Science Center
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
