UID:jk3a2m3pgu8t4dpn534ot0g0d4@google.com
CREATED:20110726T213607Z
DESCRIPTION:Haskell Workshop by Christopher Olah:\n\nHaskell is an awesome 
 purely functional language that I've been\nbecoming more and more obsessed 
 with in recent months. I consider it\nto be the most elegant language I've 
 ever worked in and want to\nintroduce more people to it!\n\nSo\, on Monday\
 , August the 8th\, 7pm/19:00 I'll be teaching an\nintroduction to Haskell w
 orkshop! Come and learn about laziness\, type\nclasses and (the awesome pow
 er of) monads!\n\nPlease note: this is not an introduction to programming c
 lass. You\nwill not be able to follow along if you don't have experience\np
 rogramming. I am planning to do a day long weekend Introduction to\nProgram
 ming/Python workshop sometime in the near future that would be\nmuch more a
 ppropriate for you.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20221122T084427Z
LOCATION:Hacklab.to\, 170A Baldwin Street\, Toronto\, Canada
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Haskell Workshop
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:HackLab.TO
DTSTART:20161204T190000Z
DTEND:20161204T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260512T040225Z
UID:o0b7h71kreggqps24frmli5ka8@google.com
CREATED:20161124T163943Z
DESCRIPTION:Hey - I've been having this conversation with numerous hacklabb
 ers\, and I'd like to scale it up a bit.  I'm interested in education refor
 m - changing that way that people learn things.  I'm not necessarily intere
 sted in just schools (though that's obviously important)\, but in consideri
 ng quite broadly the way that people learn things\, and how society can mak
 e that easier\, more accessible\, more affordable\, better\, more impactful
 \, etc.\n\nIf you're interested in that kind of thing and would like to tal
 k about it\, come join me Sunday Dec 4th at 2pm.  I don't really have an ag
 enda per say\, just curious to collect some people and have a fun discussio
 n\, perhaps with an eye towards experiments that hacklab could run on this 
 front\, or ways that we could help.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20161124T163943Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Education Reform Discussion
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
