UID:8ikhb586cfh4uf7a2lpdm8bkb8@google.com
CREATED:20150202T154224Z
DESCRIPTION:http://www.meetup.com/DIYbio-Toronto/events/220393691/\n\nAt th
 e DIYbio roundtable\, join 4 researchers for an evening of talks and discus
 sion about biology relevant to the 21st century.  \n\nOn the theme:\n\nThe 
 cost of doing biology is rapidly declining. Thanks to new technology and th
 e dropping price of DNA synthesis\, more people have access to life science
  research tools\, which opens up many possibilities for citizen science. Ac
 ademic institutions and biotech companies are no longer the only players be
 hind scientific innovation. \n\nThese facts raise interesting questions:  a
 re millions of government dollars poured into academic research the right p
 lace for them or is there a better model? What will the biology landscape l
 ook like 5 years from now?\n\nSCHEDULE:  \n\n6:30 - welcome \n7:00 - short 
 lecture by each speaker (10 mins each) \n8:00 - roundtable discussion moder
 ated by Roberta Buiani\n\nSPEAKERS AT THE EVENT\n\nAndrew Pelling is a Cana
 da Research Chair and Professor at the University of Ottawa where he direct
 s the Laboratory for Biophysical Manipulation. \n\nLaura Suen is a 26-year-
 old nuclear physicist\, science educator and television personality. She ha
 s made television appearances on CBC’s Canada’s Smartest Person\, taking th
 e title of runner-up and Canada’s smartest woman. She was also physics expe
 rt on George Stroumboulopoulos Tonight and has appeared on Discovery Channe
 l. \n\nJessie MacAlpine has been conducting research since the age of 12 in
  basements and laboratories around the world in such diverse areas as genet
 ics\, agriculture\, global health and fundamental physics. In 2014\, she wa
 s named one of Canada's Top 20 Under 20.\n\nRex Xia was the brains behind U
 ofT’s 2014 iGEM project. He studies Integrative Biology at the University o
 f Toronto.
LAST-MODIFIED:20150212T225909Z
LOCATION:Hacklab\, 1266 Queen Street West\, Toronto\, ON M6K 1L3\, Canada
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:DIYbio Roundtable: the future of biology
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
