UID:ip7929k0muvh4grn88ll1h21l8@google.com
CREATED:20130603T214540Z
DESCRIPTION:What: Hacklab Junk Independence Day #4\nWhere: Hacklab.to\, 170
 A Baldwin Street\nWhen: Sunday June 16th\, 2pm till late\nWhat: get rid of 
 your old electronics\, and hopefully walk away with somebody's else's unrec
 ognized treasures!\n\nBy popular demand\, I've scheduled the next Junk Inde
 pendence Day at Hacklab!  It'll be SUNDAY June 16th\, from 2pm till late.  
 Bring all your old electronics\, batteries\, etc.  We'll be collecting them
  in the kitchen area\, and as always\, one man's junk is another man's trea
 sure: come look through the stuff for the cool thing you've never known you
  wanted!  Our pickup (as detailed below) will be the next morning\, Shift R
 ecycling will be coming by with a truck to take it all away.\n\nEric\n\n\n\
 n-------- Original Message --------\nSubject: RE: eWaste pickup for Hacklab
 \nDate: Tue\, 4 Jun 2013 13:34:25 +0000\nFrom: Mark Kostiw <mark@shiftrecyc
 ling.com>\nTo: Eric Boyd <mrericboyd@yahoo.com>\n\n\nHi Eric\, \n\nYes we w
 ould be happy to provide a free pick up for you. \n\nI'll schedule Hacklab 
 in for Monday the 17th between 9:00 am and noon. \n\nRegards\, \n\n  ----\n
   Mark Kostiw \n\n  Shift Recycling \n  94 Fenmar Drive\, \n  Toronto\, ON\
 , M9L 1M5\n  Telephone: 416.995.4202\n  Mobile: 416.994.9393\n  Fax: 416.91
 3.1830\n  www.shiftrecycling.com \n\n\n\n-----Original Message-----\nFrom: 
 Eric Boyd [mailto:mrericboyd@yahoo.com] \nSent: Monday\, June 03\, 2013 5:4
 9 PM\nTo: Sider\, Mike\nSubject: eWaste pickup for Hacklab\n\nHey\, hacklab
  would like to schedule another eWaste pickup day.  How does Monday June 17
 th (preferably in the morning) work for you?  As before we'd have about 500
  pounds of stuff so we'd like the free pickup option.\n\nHacklab.to\n170A B
 aldwin Street (in Kensington Market)\n\nEric\nPresident\, Hacklab.to\n\n\n\
 n
LAST-MODIFIED:20221122T084346Z
LOCATION:Hacklab.to\, 170A Baldwin Street
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Hacklab Junk Independence Day
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
