CREATED:20110106T231439Z
DESCRIPTION:$free\n\nWhat is LaTeX? LaTeX is a text markup language\; inste
 ad of typing in word processor like MS Word or Open Office\, you type in pl
 ain text and then compile it to a format of your choice\, such as PDF or DV
 I (HTML is implemented but kind of sketchy). Unlike HTML\, LaTeX is not ter
 ribly cumbersome to type by hand.\n\nLaTeX is the industry standard for mat
 h and science publication. Look at a random math paper or book\, at you can
  be very confident it was written in LaTeX. But LaTeX is also capable of do
 ing many things other than writing papers\, including slideshows and poster
 s. Here's an example\, a sideshow I made in grade 11:\n\nhttp://christopher
 olah.files.wordpress.com/2011/01/meme.pdf\n\nAs another example\, I made th
 is image in LaTeX for digimer:\n\nhttp://wiki.alteeve.com/index.php/File:Sa
 mpleXen2NodeClusterMap.png\n\nThis workshop is only an introduction. By the
  end you will be able to create simple documents and typeset equations. If 
 there is time and interest\, I will go into how to make slideshows and the 
 basics of diagrams.\n\ncolah\nhttp://christopherolah.wordpress.com/
LAST-MODIFIED:20221122T084202Z
LOCATION:Hacklab.to\, 170A Baldwin Street\, Toronto\, Canada
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Hacklab: LaTeX Workshop
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
