BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:HackLab.TO
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20171024T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20171024T230000
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;UNTIL=20180313T212959Z;INTERVAL=1;BYDAY=TU
DTSTAMP:20260512T040225Z
UID:05D4930A-2992-4AF7-9190-5462A732312C
CREATED:20180310T171407Z
DESCRIPTION:Every Tuesday\, from around 6 pm until late\, the lab opens up 
 our front door to members of the public. We’re specifically excited about f
 olks who want to show off projects they have made or are working on\, want 
 to ask for help with making something awesome\, or want to help out on othe
 r folks’ projects. Bringing a laptop along to just chill out with other gee
 ks is also welcome.\n\nThere’s no minimum skill level required to participa
 te\, and we do our best to be a respectful\, friendly environment for every
 one. Regretfully we are not wheelchair accessible – there are steps leading
  up to the floor the lab is on. As a heads-up to folks with sensory process
 ing issues\, the Tuesdays can get quite busy and noisy. 7 to 9 pm tends to 
 be the busiest time\, but in our new larger space there are usually places 
 you can get away from it.\n\nMembers of the media are also welcome\, but in
