UID:ci1a2tte6a6fd7s09pu2q0lhcs@google.com
CREATED:20111212T231557Z
DESCRIPTION:The Basic Electronics Class is designed to help Arduino hackers
  and beginner electronics enthusiasts learn some of the important theory an
 d terminology that everyone needs to know. The first set of three classes w
 ill attempt to cover as many fundamentals as possible. If you're confused b
 y ohms law\, how to choose and use basic components\, or even what basic el
 ectronic components are used for\, this is the class for you!\n\nBring gene
 ral electronics questions\, or project ideas as the second half of each cla
 ss will be an open discussion about electronics topics.\n\nThe class will b
 e taught by Andrew Kilpatrick. Andrew has designed all kinds of electronics
  including his own line of musical equipment: www.kilpatrickaudio.com Andre
 w has been involved with Hacklab Toronto since 2008. 
LAST-MODIFIED:20221122T084140Z
LOCATION:Hacklab\, 170A Baldwin Street\, Toronto
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Basic Electronics Class
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:HackLab.TO
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20150319T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20150319T220000
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;UNTIL=20150319T230000Z;BYDAY=TH
DTSTAMP:20260512T040225Z
UID:2jhacgjr2qrr4s8rbo2qamootk@google.com
CREATED:20150319T224212Z
DESCRIPTION:Existential risks are threats to our future. Examples include n
 uclear war\, some (possibly engineered) extremely lethal disease\, and thre
 ats due to emerging technologies.\n\nhttp://www.existential-risk.org/concep
 t.html\n\nThe effective altruism movement is a friendly alliance containing
  those who see existential risk as a top priority together with those favou
 ring more conventional causes such as poverty alleviation and animal rights
 .\n\nThe question to think about for this meeting is: is it sane and altrui
 stic to try to reduce existential risk?\n\nSub-problems:\n\n- how morally r
 elevant are the vast number of potential future generations?\n\n- which exi
 stential risks do we focus on?\n\n- how do we make existential risk reducti
 on tractable?\n\n- in particular\, how do we measure the risk of something 
 that hasn't happened yet? How do we know we're reducing it?\n\n- overall\, 
 how does xrisk weigh against other areas of EA interest?\n\nAlso worth givi
 ng a shout-out to http://gcrinstitute.org/\n\n\nHacklab space: Ten Forward 
 (if DIYbio isn't using it) otherwise Classroom\nAll are welcome!
LAST-MODIFIED:20150326T150442Z
LOCATION:Hacklab\, 1266 Queen Street West\, Toronto\, ON M6K 1L3\, Canada
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Effective Altruism - LessWrong Rationality Meetup
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
