CREATED:20120331T220207Z
DESCRIPTION:Sen and I are planning on holding a Stitch 'n Bitch on April 9t
 h @ 6PM. For those of you who don't know what that means\, it means we will
  be having a 'fabric hacking' meet-up for sewers\, stitchers\, fabric-spinn
 ers\, knitters and all other forms of fabric hacking. Sewing is one of the 
 oldest forms of making and hacking in all of human-kind\, so we figured it'
 d be a great idea to introduce it to Hacklab in a more official way. \n\nBr
 ing your gear or ask someone to share theirs with you! This is a general ev
 ent and not a tutorial. We're hoping a good number of people can show up to
  just talk about and exchange tips on fabric hacking. \n\nThis is an open e
 vent for Hacklab members and anyone who is interested. :)
LAST-MODIFIED:20221122T083613Z
LOCATION:Hacklab.to\, 170A Baldwin Street\, Toronto
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Stitch and Bitch
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
