UID:duumaepmedt0oggrg1v8rkcajg@google.com
CREATED:20140502T184557Z
DESCRIPTION:http://hackaday.io/prize/mission\n\nSo\, hackaday is offering $
 196\,418 (apparently it's a Fibonacci number) to the best group that "build
 s the next evolution of hardware".  No doubt hundreds of teams will partici
 pate.  The big requirement seems to be that the thing is a "connected devic
 e"\, and connectedness is meaningful to the function.  So\, basically\, int
 ernet of things contest.\n\nI hereby propose that hacklab has a team\, let'
 s get hacking!  The first deadline is June 27th\, and basically you have to
  have a two minute video describing your entry and some profile information
 . That gives us about 2 months to come up with our idea and make it awesome
  sounding.\n\nBrainstorming session: SUNDAY MAY 18th\, 2-4pm.  Come on out 
 and let's see if can we think up something awesome.  I've got some ideas ly
 ing around (like upgrades to my Heart Spark\, or the Luma Droid)\, but I'm 
 sure we can do better together!  It's a super wide open canvas\, so almost 
 anything goes.  After the brainstorming session\, we'll schedule a hackatho
 n\, and start assembling the stuff we'll need to build at least a mockup th
 at we could film for the first deadline. 
LAST-MODIFIED:20140502T184629Z
LOCATION:Hacklab\, 170A Baldwin Street\, Toronto
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Hackaday Prize Brainstorming
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
