BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:HackLab.TO
DTSTART:20160525T230000Z
DTEND:20160526T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260512T040225Z
UID:5p6c1handqd5t2ko6fk62063eo@google.com
CREATED:20160501T155132Z
DESCRIPTION:Workshop Workshop is a hands-on training session for people\, g
 roups or organizations looking to plan events workshops or happenings\, wit
 h an emphasis on hands on workshops in the maker community. This workshop w
 ill take learners through the process from clearly imagining their workshop
  to planning it’s logistics. There will be tips and resources for getting w
 hat you need and how to ask for what you want to make any event run smoothl
 y. \n\nThis event is run in collaboration with Maker Festival to facilitate
  satellite events alongside the festival\, however these things apply to an
 y of your endeavors.  \n\nIn this workshop we will: \n\n    Work through th
 e planning of a hypothetical event for the purpose of the workshop process\
 n\n    Identify personal objectives in running an event\n\n    Set the goal
 s and expectations for the event and audience\n\n    Define the technical n
 eeds of your workshop\n\n    Explore ways to find appropriate venues\n\n   
  How to approach sponsorship for your event\n\n    Practice facilitation te
 chniques  \n\n    We will provide consultation and aide for your actual eve
 nt during Maker Festival using our contacts and resources\n\nIf you are pla
 nning to run an event\, or have an idea of an event you would like to see e
 xist\, come to Workshop Workshop and learn how to make it real! \n\nHOW MUC
 H: 20$ suggested donation (PWYC at the door\, no one turned away)\n\nHOW MA
 NY PEOPLE: 20-25
LAST-MODIFIED:20160526T033414Z
LOCATION:Hacklab\, 1266 Queen Street West #6\, Toronto\, ON\, Canada
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Workshop Workshop
TRANSP:OPAQUE
