DTSTART:20131214T190000Z
DTEND:20131214T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260512T040225Z
UID:uhle6267f9vam2naf1i3ti54uk@google.com
CREATED:20131205T194053Z
DESCRIPTION:Subtle Technologies Call for Submissions is out.  This year the
 ir theme is "Open Culture: Participatory Practices in Art & Science". Obvio
 usly hacklab has related interests.  The festival is usually a crazy batch 
 of really different things submitted by artists and scientists - they do no
 t just talks\, but workshops\, demos\, performances\, etc.\n\nhttp://subtle
 technologies.com/festival/call-for-submissions/\n\nSo\, I'm thinking we sho
 uld do a brainstorming meeting at hacklab.  The deadline is January 20th\, 
 so we've got a bit of time\, but I don't want to wait until after Christmas
 .  If you're interested in talking about what hacklab might do\, please com
 e to this meeting: Saturday December 14th at 2-4pm.  We'll just talk at a f
 airly high level about how hacklab might participate\, bat some ideas aroun
 d\, and see if we can find a super fun thing to do.\n\nSome brief ideas:\n 
 - we could lead workshops at the festival\, e.g. soldering\, arduino\, Rasp
 Pi\, etc.\n - manage group tour slots for festival attendees\, to come see 
 our space\n - do a hackathon at the festival to build something cool\, fest
 ival attendees welcome to participate\n - an exhibition of our stuff at the
  festival (similar to e.g. mini maker faire table)\n - etc.etc.\n\nIf you'r
 e interested\, please come on out to the meeting!  Sat Dec 14th\, 2-4pm.\n\
 nEric\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20131205T194100Z
LOCATION:Hacklab\,to\, 170A Baldwin Street\, Toronto
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Subtle Tech Brainstorm
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
