BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:HackLab.TO
DTSTART:20120303T190000Z
DTEND:20120303T220000Z
DTSTAMP:20260512T040225Z
UID:0hcm2d96g3bkun46vm7h25anlg@google.com
CREATED:20120224T154008Z
DESCRIPTION:I've talked to several people about this\, so I know some peopl
 e are\ninterested\, and I though I would open it up.  I want to build a\nca
 mera-carrying quadcopter (or hexa-copter\, etc) this spring\, so that I can
 \nfly it this summer.  I want to be able to take videos like this one:\n\nh
 ttp://www.youtube.com/watch?feature=player_embedded&v=bsrzBwylodU\n\nI beli
 eve to get video like this\, you have to transmit the video back to the\nop
 erator - otherwise it's very difficult to navigate in this way.  Note that\
 nthe operator of the above quadcopter actually has heads-up video goggles\,
 \nfor true immersive flight experience!\n\nhttp://www.gowiththeshark.com/\n
 \nObviously this isn't a small or cheap project.  I'm open to collaboration
 \nand sharing.  Most specifically\, I'm looking for other people who also w
 ant\nto do something like this\, and we'll form a team.  We'll figure out w
 hat we\nwant to build\, build at least one of them\, and share the fun (and
  also the\ncosts).  If we had many people\, I think it would be cool to bui
 ld two or\nmore so that we could have spy-vs-spy contests or whatever.  So 
 yeah\,\nbasically I'm thinking: Toronto Quadcopters Users Group.\n\nAgenda 
 for the first meeting:\n - explore our quadcopter options: figure out what 
 products\, kits or open source designs are available\, try to get price inf
 o & stats for each\n - explore our "wireless video camera" options: ditto.\
 n - investigate legal stuff\n - talk about budget\, sharing\, division of l
 abor\, project timeline\, etc.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20221122T083623Z
LOCATION:Hacklab.to\, 170A Baldwin Street\, Toronto
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Quadcopter Building Group Meeting
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
