CREATED:20131212T211331Z
DESCRIPTION:What: Hacklab Junk Independence Day #5\nWhere: Hacklab.to\, 170
 A Baldwin Street\nWhen: Sunday January 12th\, 2pm till late\nWhat: get rid 
 of your old electronics\, and hopefully walk away with somebody's else's un
 recognized treasures!\n\nBy popular demand\, I've scheduled the next Junk I
 ndependence Day at Hacklab!  It'll be SUNDAY January 12th\, from 2pm till l
 ate.  Bring all your old electronics\, batteries\, etc.  We'll be collectin
 g them in the kitchen area\, and as always\, one man's junk is another man'
 s treasure: come look through the stuff for the cool thing you've never kno
 wn you wanted!  Our pickup (as detailed below) will be the next morning\, S
 hift Recycling will be coming by with a truck to take it all away.\n\nEric\
 n\n\nOn 12/12/13 4:24 PM\, Mark Kostiw wrote:\n> Hey Eric\n>\n> I have you 
 booked in for Monday a.m.\, Jan. 13\, 2014.  If anything changes let us kno
 w!\n>\n> All the best\,\n>\n> Mark\n>\n>\n> _______________________________
 _________\n> From: Eric Boyd [mrericboyd@yahoo.com]\n> Sent: Thursday\, Dec
 ember 12\, 2013 4:13 PM\n> To: Sider\, Mike\n> Subject: eWaste pickup for h
 acklab\n>\n> Hey\, hacklab would like to schedule another eWaste pickup day
 .  How does\n> Monday January 13th (preferably in the morning) work for you
 ? As before\n> we'd have about 500 pounds of stuff so we'd like the free pi
 ckup option.\n>\n> Hacklab\, 170A Baldwin Street\, in Kensington Market.\n>
 \n> Eric\n>\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20131217T212706Z
LOCATION:Hacklab\, 170A Baldwin Street\, Toronto
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Hacklab Junk Independence Day
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
