CREATED:20180103T035328Z
DESCRIPTION:**Eventbrite https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/arduino-for-beginners-
 tickets-41774536764**\n\nPWYC/FREE ADMISSION Arduino Beginners Workshop [pa
 rts extra]. For total beginners. All are welcome. A-Train and Zach will sho
 w you how to get started with Arduino\, the super-friendly microcontroller 
 platform that even artists love. We’ll cover getting the software installed
  and going\, hooking up the Arduino\, and a little bit of basic programming
 \, via explanation of the Examples. You too can cut and paste your way to a
  working project!\n***If you can't bring your own Arduino (any kind will do
 ) and any cables required to attach it to your laptop (typically an A to B 
 USB cable)\, we'll be selling kits for $10. You'll also need a laptop on wh
 ich you can install software. You can purchase an Arduino at Creatron at  3
 49 College St\, Toronto\, ON M5T 1S5 (or online\, of course). The Arduino U
 no is the recommended board for beginners\, but any arduino will do if you 
 have a more specialized project in mind.***\nFinding Hacklab: We're at Quee
 n and Dufferin\, NW corner\, buzz unit #12.
LAST-MODIFIED:20180202T021152Z
LOCATION:Hacklab\, 1266 Queen Street West #12\, Toronto\, ON\, Canada
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Arduino Beginners Workshop with ATrain and Zach
TRANSP:OPAQUE
