UID:n05nie6mo197poihc00vngi81g@google.com
CREATED:20170124T000521Z
DESCRIPTION:I will disassemble left nozzle of Flashforge printer and will a
 ttempt to clean it.\n\nThen I will refill left nozze with Orange PLA fillam
 ent from Monoprice.\n\nThen I will set up the bed to use Kapton Tape from M
 onoprice.\n\n\nInfo on cleaning nozzle and extruder (from the mailing list)
 :\n\nDrive gear and extruder basics -- http://toms3d.org/2016/04/15/build-y
 our-own-3d-printer-everything-about-extruders/\n\nBasics: Cleaning out a cl
 ogged nozzle -- https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=g8uvh6kvr54\n\nCleaning the
  Extruder Drive Gear on a FlashForge Creator Pro 3D printer -- https://www.
 youtube.com/watch?v=vmIY9_6s8Ss\n\nFlashForge Creator Pro ABS nozzle cleani
 ng -- https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=x3yp6H4D_ao\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20170124T000521Z
LOCATION:Hacklab Classroom
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Flashforge Nozzle cleaning
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:HackLab.TO
DTSTART:20150127T000000Z
DTEND:20150127T020000Z
DTSTAMP:20260512T040225Z
UID:rkgr7pjgp699srrhn4jgogl3jo@google.com
CREATED:20150118T212143Z
DESCRIPTION:http://hacklab-arduino-11.eventbrite.ca\n\nArduino Beginners Wo
 rkshop. For total beginners. All are welcome. Eric will show you how to get
  started with Arduino\, the super-friendly microcontroller platform that ev
 en artists love. We’ll cover getting the software installed and going\, hoo
 king up the Arduino\, and a little bit of basic programming\, via explanati
 on of the Examples. You too can cut and paste your way to a working project
 !\n***You’ll need to bring your own Arduino (any kind will do) and a laptop
  on which you can install software. Also please bring any cables required t
 o attach your Arduino to your laptop – typically this means an A to B USB c
 able. If you do not have an Arduino\, you can purchase one at Creatron at 2
 55 College Street (or online\, of course).  The Arduino Uno is the recommen
 ded board for beginners\, but any arduino will do if you have a more specia
 lized project in mind.***\nFinding Hacklab: We're at Queen and Dufferin\, N
 W corner\, buzz unit #12.\nA PWCY (pay what you can) donation of $10 is sug
 gested.  Nobody turned away for lack of funds.
