BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:HackLab.TO
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20140916T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20140916T230000
DTSTAMP:20260512T040225Z
UID:0680F968-6904-49B8-B55B-5E01B3078F7A
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Toronto:20140916T173000
CREATED:20130918T114927Z
DESCRIPTION:Every Tuesday\, from around 6pm until late\, the lab opens up o
 ur front door to members of the public. We’re specifically excited about fo
 lks who want to show off projects they have made or are working on\, want t
 o ask for help with making something awesome\, or want to help out on other
  folks’ projects. Bringing a laptop along to just chill out with other geek
 s is also welcome.\n\nThere’s no minimal skill level required to participat
 e\, and we do our best to be a respectful\, friendly environment for everyo
 ne. Regretfully we are not wheelchair accessible – there are 17 steps leadi
 ng up to the lab\, and 2 steps up to the bathroom. As a heads-up to folks w
 ith sensory processing issues\, the Tuesdays can get quite busy and noisy. 
 7 to 8 pm tends to be the busiest time.\n\nMembers of the media are also we
 lcome\, but in the interest of member privacy we have cute little press pas
 ses hanging by the door\, and require that permission be sought before taki
 ng photos with people in them.
LAST-MODIFIED:20171019T153009Z
LOCATION:170A Baldwin St.
SEQUENCE:13
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:HackLab.TO Open House
TRANSP:OPAQUE
