BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:HackLab.TO
DTSTART:20231202T190000Z
DTEND:20231202T220000Z
DTSTAMP:20260512T040225Z
UID:6jdcbtcnhakdkdpvfur28ha3i2@google.com
CREATED:20231117T173055Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Hacklabbers Welcome!  Please also RSVP on the meetup so that
  we can get a feel for how many people are coming.</p><p>From the Meetup Ev
 ent: <a href="https://www.meetup.com/toronto-solarpunk-meetup/events/297422
 713/">https://www.meetup.com/toronto-solarpunk-meetup/events/297422713/</a>
  </p><p>Let's play<span> </span><a href="https://thefuture.wtf/">Solarpunk 
 Futures</a><span> </span>together! Here's what the creators say about the g
 ame:</p><p>"Solarpunk Futures is a storytelling game where players imagine 
 the pathways to a desirable world from the perspective of a utopian future.
  Players use a deck of cards to remember Ancestors and work together using 
 Tools and Values to overcome a set of real-world Challenges. Through dialog
 ue and collaborative worldbuilding\, collective and visionary narratives em
 erge of a new society\, along with plausible scenarios for how to get there
 ."</p><p>They<span> </span><a href="https://thefuture.wtf/workshop.html">al
 so say</a><span> </span>on the workshop page that "this is not a competitiv
 e game"\, "this is a political game". Between 1-8 people can play\, the ide
 al is 3-6\, and that it takes 45 minutes. Probably our first play-through w
 ill take an hour or a bit more\, since we'll be reading the rules and learn
 ing. If we have more than 8 people show up\, I will also be bringing<span> 
 </span><a href="https://boardgamegeek.com/boardgame/140934/arboretum">Arbor
 etum</a>\, which is a surprisingly engaging game of arranging trees (it's v
 ery solarpunk)\, it takes a similar amount of time\, we can have two groups
  which swap position after the first play of each.</p><p>I've never actuall
 y played Solarpunk Futures myself\, I bought it to mine it for ideas for my
  Solarpunk Tarot deck project. But I'd love to try it\, just be forewarned:
  I am expecting it to more like a short D&amp\;D campaign than like a board
  game experience. You'll be collaboratively telling stories in a solarpunk 
 future with the other players.</p><p>I'm also keen to do the extra-credit q
 uestions they mention at the end of the workshop page: "Debrief: what happe
 ned briefly? anything prominent that came up? Further discussion about: Wha
 t did your utopia look like? How did it feel? What will you take to your ow
 n life/organizing work? Could Solarpunk Futures be useful in your organizin
 g work?"</p><p>If you've got other solarpunk-themed board games or anything
  like that\, please bring those too\, and we can make a whole afternoon out
  of it!</p><p>Also\, pursuant to our discussion in the last meeting\, if yo
 u've got home-made snacks\, food\, or beverages to share\, please bring and
  we can all enjoy!</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20231202T183847Z
LOCATION:Hacklab\, 1677 St Clair Ave W\, Toronto\, ON M6N 1H9\, Canada
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Solarpunk Futures gaming day
TRANSP:OPAQUE
