CREATED:20120217T203940Z
DESCRIPTION:$free\, RSVP at:\nhttp://polyglotsecrets.eventbrite.com\n\nThin
 king of learning French to impress your boyfriend or girlfriend? Or wanting
  to learn Spanish to start a business in Mexico?\n\nJoin us on March 5th (M
 onday) and get tips and tricks of learning multiple spoken languages. You w
 ill learn how to tackle a new language and gain confidence to succeed.\n\nF
 ramework:\n   - Motivation: Why you want to learn [_YourLanguage_]?\n   - P
 arts of a Language: Leverage your strengths\n   - General Grammar: almost a
 ll languages share similar features\n   - Language Family Tree\n   - How to
  estimate how much time you need to learn a language? Self-evaluation.\n   
 - Finding Resources\n \nThe Polyglot Framework will be taught by Chim of Mi
 belo. He speaks seven languages (French\, Portuguese\, English\, Cantonese\
 , Mandarin\, Swedish and Spanish).
LAST-MODIFIED:20221122T083731Z
LOCATION:hacklab.to\, 170A Baldwin Street\, Toronto
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Polyglot - Tips and Tricks to Learn Multiple Languages
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:HackLab.TO
DTSTART:20131112T000000Z
DTEND:20131112T020000Z
DTSTAMP:20260512T040225Z
UID:jlbrdhrjbcie4imcpe2bi5mlkg@google.com
CREATED:20131005T192835Z
DESCRIPTION:For Hacklab Members\nhttps://cadsoft-eagle-tutorial.eventbrite.
 com/\n\nCome learn CADsoft Eagle\, "award winning software [that] offers us
 er friendly\, powerful and affordable solutions for PCB design\, including 
 Schematic Capture\, Board Layout and Autorouter."  It's used by many hobbyi
 sts thanks to the free version\, which isn't horribly crippled\, and it's u
 sed by Spark Fun\, so many open source PCB designs are already available an
 d easy to copy from!   The tutorial will be in three parts\, over three con
 secutive Mondays:\n\nMonday March 19th: Schematic Capture.  Taking your cir
 cuit schematic and laying it out in Eagle\, including things like adding pa
 rts\, wiring parts\, and naming things.  ERC electrical rule check.\n\nMond
 ay March 26th: PCB Layout.  Including part placement and routing of signals
 .  Trace thickness\, autorouting\, layers\, and DRC design rule check.\n\nM
 onday April 2nd:  CAM Processor\, Ordering Boards & using the Parts Editor.
   Using the CAM processor to create Gerbers (the data files that all board 
 houses accept).  Quick review of some PCB making services.  Creating a new 
 part.  Copying and editing an existing part.  Library management.  \n\nAtte
 ndees should come to all three sessions\, to get complete coverage of Eagle
 .  So make sure you are available for all sessions before signing up.  Plea
 se download and install Eagle before the first session.\n\nThe tutorial wil
 l be taught by Eric and Sen\, we both have years of experience using Eagle 
 to make PCBs for shipping products.  
LAST-MODIFIED:20131005T192916Z
LOCATION:Hacklab.TO\, 170A Baldwin Street\, Toronto
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:CadSOFT Eagle Workshop: Schematic Capture
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
