CREATED:20171213T215309Z
DESCRIPTION:Canadian Space Society: UofT astronomy graduate student Emily D
 eibert will be speaking about exoplanet atmospheres.\n\nVenus Labs Brainsto
 rming Session: A 30-minute exercise during which we will come up with as ma
 ny ideas as possible (there are no bad ideas) for initial missions or techn
 ological developments which will aid in the mission of the Venus Labs.  The
  ultimate desire is to colonize the planet Venus using "cloud cities"\, buo
 yant structures that colonists will live inside\, floating in the habitable
 -zone about 54km above the surface.  But Rome wasn't built in a day\, we ne
 ed some ideas on what to do now to work towards this mission.  Both technol
 ogical and sociological ideas are needed!
LAST-MODIFIED:20180201T011421Z
LOCATION:Hacklab\, 1266 Queen St W\, Toronto\, ON M6K 1L3\, Canada
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:VenusLabs Meeting
TRANSP:OPAQUE
