BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:HackLab.TO
DTSTART:20181013T180000Z
DTEND:20181013T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260512T040225Z
UID:5f6ktf896735n5uqc0o2e3cioi@google.com
CREATED:20180912T213629Z
DESCRIPTION:https://www.meetup.com/Long-Now-Toronto/events/254627578\n\nThe
  Long Now Foundation is holding a special even in San Francisco to celebrat
 e the 50th anniversary of the Whole Earth Catalog. I (your organizer Eric B
 oyd) personally am too young to have experienced it at the time\, but I did
  read a lot about that time\, and I have a copy of the Last Whole Earth Cat
 alog\, which I purchased from eBay many years ago. Let's meetup and talk ab
 out this iconic work - it's such a pleasure just to flip through it\, so if
  you've never seen it\, that alone will be worth the trip. If you have othe
 r copies/editions\, please bring them too! We'll also have a wide-ranging d
 iscussion about the philosophy behind the Catalog\, and what modern day pro
 jects bear any resemblance to it ("World Changing: a users guide to the 21s
 t century" is the only one I can think of\, and that was over 10 years ago 
 now). Does eBay itself reflect a modern Catalog? How about YouTube? Is ther
 e ANY modern example of the positivity that the Catalog possessed? If not\,
  why not?
LAST-MODIFIED:20181013T183255Z
LOCATION:Hacklab.TO - 1266 Queen Street West #6 - Toronto\, ON\, ca
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Whole Earth Catalog 50th Anniversary
TRANSP:OPAQUE
