CREATED:20180103T035414Z
DESCRIPTION:**Eventbrite link TBA**\n\nArduino Beginners Workshop [parts ex
 tra]. For total beginners. All are welcome. $20 includes all fees + starter
  Arduino kit.\nA-Train and Zach will show you how to get started with Ardui
 no\, the super-friendly microcontroller platform that even artists love. We
 ’ll cover getting the software installed and going\, hooking up the Arduino
 \, and a little bit of basic programming\, via explanation of the Examples.
  You too can cut and paste your way to a working project!\n***If you can't 
 bring your own Arduino (any kind will do) and any cables required to attach
  it to your laptop (typically an A to B USB cable)\, we'll be selling kits 
 included with the price of admission. You'll also need a laptop on which yo
 u can install software. You can purchase an Arduino at Creatron at  349 Col
 lege St\, Toronto\, ON M5T 1S5 (or online\, of course). The Arduino Uno is 
 the recommended board for beginners\, but any arduino will do if you have a
  more specialized project in mind.***\nFinding Hacklab: We're at Queen and 
 Dufferin\, NW corner\, buzz unit #12.
LAST-MODIFIED:20180420T001647Z
LOCATION:Hacklab\, 1266 Queen Street West #12\, Toronto\, ON\, Canada
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Arduino Beginners Workshop with ATrain & Zach
