CREATED:20100315T135317Z
DESCRIPTION:The Feigenbaum delta constant is roughly 4.66920160910299067185
 320382...\nSince it arises in chaos theory (and because there is no April 6
 6)\, it\nseems most fitting to use the Discordian calendar\, and celebrate\
 nFeigenbaum delta day on the 66th day of Bureaucracy at 9:20:16.  We are go
 ing with PM\, since most people will be working during the AM.\n\nConvertin
 g to the Gregorian calendar\, Wikipedia reports that Bureflux\,\nwhich is t
 he 50th day of Bureaucracy corresponds to the Gregorian day of\nSeptember 2
 6\, so October 1\, being 5 days later\, would be Bureaucracy 55\,\nand addi
 ng 11 days to get to Bureaucracy 66 (i.e. 4.66) brings us to\nOctober 12 (w
 hich\, this year\, is a Tuesday!).
LAST-MODIFIED:20221122T084456Z
LOCATION:Hacklab
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Feigenbaum delta day
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
