BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:HackLab.TO
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20160314T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20160314T210000
DTSTAMP:20260512T040225Z
UID:7rq3nl49njd7r0a4f7g7abrqns@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Toronto:20160314T190000
CREATED:20160116T205258Z
DESCRIPTION:REGISTRATION: https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/hacklab-cadsoft-eagle
 -tutorial-tickets-20834821512\n\nCome learn CADsoft Eagle\, "award winning 
 software [that] offers user friendly\, powerful and affordable solutions fo
 r PCB design\, including Schematic Capture\, Board Layout and Autorouter." 
  It's used by many hobbyists thanks to the free version\, which isn't horri
 bly crippled\, and it's used by Spark Fun\, so many open source PCB designs
  are already available and easy to copy from!   The tutorial will be in thr
 ee parts\, over three consecutive Mondays.\n\nAttendees should come to all 
 three sessions\, to get complete coverage of Eagle.  So make sure you are a
 vailable for all sessions before signing up.  Please download and install E
 agle before the first session.\n\nThe tutorial will be taught by Eric and S
 en\, we both have years of experience using Eagle to make PCBs for shipping
  products. \n \nNOTE: the interface is confusing\, you need only one ticket
 \, just pick the first date from the dropdown\, and you'll be registered fo
 r all three dates of the event.\nSuggested donation to the HackLab of $10/n
 ight\, or PWYC. This helps the lab keep our doors open and run lots more wo
 rkshops like this one!\n\nWeek One: Schematic Capture.  Taking your circuit
  schematic and laying it out in Eagle\, including things like adding parts\
 , wiring parts\, and naming things.  ERC electrical rule check.
LAST-MODIFIED:20160314T224307Z
LOCATION:Hacklab\, 1266 Queen St W\, Toronto\, ON M6K 1L3\, Canada
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:CADsoft Eagle Tutorial
TRANSP:OPAQUE
