DESCRIPTION:Message Body:\nMy name is Greg Astill and I work at the Toronto
  reference Library in the Digital Design Studio.  We're hoping to enhance w
 hat we already offer to the public and we love what you guys are doing over
  at the Hacklab.\n\nI am currently a member of a task group that has been p
 ut together to conduct a needs assessment and more importantly identify tec
 hnology we can incorporate into our space.\n\nThe team would like to know i
 f it's possible to set up a meeting/visit and come on down and speak to som
 eone and get more info\, and get some questions answered.\n\nI appreciate y
 our time and thank you in advance.\n\nSincerely\,\nGreg Astill\nDigital Des
 ign Studio Technician
LAST-MODIFIED:20130220T175149Z
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, 789 Young Street\, Toronto
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:tour Digital Design Studio at Toronto Reference Library
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:HackLab.TO
DTSTART:20180109T000000Z
DTEND:20180109T030000Z
DTSTAMP:20260512T040225Z
UID:4kbilmgq2lio20p1o9lta521hp@google.com
CREATED:20171208T032421Z
DESCRIPTION:https://www.facebook.com/events/382152362223334/\n\nThe first C
 areer Explorations meetup went so well\, we're going to have another one ea
 rly in January! \n\nIt’ll be a great chance to think and talk about goal-se
 tting for 2018\, and for discussing anything else career-related that you’d
  like to bring up. Possible topics\, some of which came up at the first mee
 ting:\n- How to shape a coherent narrative about your career when your jobs
  and education have been all over the place\n- Scary career decisions: Stay
  in a secure but stifling job\, or follow an exciting opportunity that migh
 t not pan out?\n- How can you tap into the invisible job market? \n- What d
 oes success really mean to you? \n- What if you know where you want to go\,
  but don't know how to get there? \n- What are the trends in your industry 
 or areas of interest?\n- And\, of course\, how can negotiation and conflict
  resolution strategies come in handy as you navigate career challenges? \n\
 nIt’ll be an informal conversation\; if there are lots of people\, we’ll br
 eak out into smaller discussion groups. \n\nEric Boyd has kindly offered to
  host at Hacklab.TO\, so as a bonus\, there will be a chance to check out t
 he laser cutter\, 3D printers\, and other neato maker-space equipment!\n\n-
 - \n\nNote: this event is part of the "How to Talk to People about Things" 
 facebook Alumni group.  Hacklab members are welcome.
LAST-MODIFIED:20180108T235840Z
LOCATION:Hacklab Classroom
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Career Explorations Meetup at Hacklab
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-APPLE-TRAVEL-ADVISORY-BEHAVIOR:AUTOMATIC
