UID:umj95uiteen8clarkavf7cq4ks@google.com
CREATED:20161201T213654Z
DESCRIPTION:https://www.meetup.com/Long-Now-Toronto/events/235967654/\n\nLe
 t's get together and talk about our Personal Long Now's.  Every year I do s
 ome kind of project for New Year's\, and this year I've been thinking a lot
  about creative career design and how I want to impact the world.  Come joi
 n me for a salon where we talk about what one person can accomplish over th
 e long term.  What's worth accomplishing?  What will most affect the future
  of humanity? \n\nHere's bit of food for thought: if you compare the size o
 r lifespan of a human to the universe\, humans are MUCH more powerful in ti
 me than they are in space\, i.e. 100/14 billion years is much better than 2
 m/91 billion light years.  In fact by that metric\, we're billions of times
  more powerful in time than we are in space.  So: let's leverage that!\n\nA
 lso\, there will be a discussion of the best SALT from this year (please co
 me prepared with your favorite!).  Here's a list of 2016 talks (in reverse 
 chronological order) for your reference:\n\nLost Landscapes of San Francisc
 o #11\, Rick Prelinger \nThe Extreme Present\, Douglas Coupland \nThe Brain
  and the Now\, David Eagleman \nThe Well Tempered City\, Jonathan Rose \nQu
 antum Computer Reality\, Seth Lloyd \nThe Next 30 Digital Years\, Kevin Kel
 ly \nAlgorithms to Live By\, Brian Christian \nThe Marshmallow Test: Master
 ing Self-Control\, Walter Mischel \nSolving Dark Matter and Dark Energy\, P
 riyamvada Natarajan \nRadical Ag: C4 Rice and Beyond\, Jane Langdale \nFire
  Fast\, Fire Slow\, Fire Deep\, Stephen Pyne \n1177 B.C. When Civilization 
 Collapsed\, Eric Cline
LAST-MODIFIED:20170104T233809Z
LOCATION:Hacklab\, 1266 Queen St W\, Toronto\, ON M6K 1L3\, Canada
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Personal Long Now Salon
TRANSP:OPAQUE
