UID:0unkgm774s2jt6t4o6l6utbrbo@google.com
CREATED:20141015T210227Z
DESCRIPTION:The folks over at Storage Wars Canada found some lockpicks in a
  storage locker\, and want to shoot a segment about them.  A former member 
 who is friends with one of their staff emailed the lab and asked if anyone 
 might be interested in helping them out\, and it just so happens that I’m (
 Nicholas Dodd) a certified Locksmith.  After chatting with them a bit\, the
 y want to shoot a segment at the Hacklab\, learn a bit of lockpicking and c
 heck the space out.  They also like the open-house atmosphere\, so clearly 
 this is cause for a public event!\n\nWhen: Monday\, October 20 2014\, 2pm –
  6pm\nWhere: Hacklab.to\, 1266 Queen Street West Toronto\nPlease use the bu
 zzer at the front door to be let in when you arrive.\n \nThis will be a lot
  like an open-house\, so bring your projects and computers like normal\, th
 ough if you have an interest in lockpicking you should bring your picking g
 ear and interesting practice locks.  If you don’t know how to pick but want
  to learn\, you should bring your sense of curiosity!\nSince this is a comm
 ercial shoot\, we ask the attendees all agree to the following:\nShow up ar
 ound 2pm — actual filming will begin around 3ish.\nBe willing to sign a wai
 ver from Storage Wars saying you’re okay with being filmed.\nNot wear any l
 arge identifiable logos or brand-names (small logos which can be taped over
  are okay).\nBe willing to take minor directions from the film crew and dir
 ector while in the space — they may want to move people from room to room f
 or instance\, or have everyone relocate to one table.\nWe look forward to s
 eeing you there!  If you have any other questions about this event\, please
  email info@hacklab.to
