UID:dtvu1gl9qbrtt97n51untj8j7o@google.com
CREATED:20140408T204657Z
DESCRIPTION:Hi Eric\,\n\nI am following up with you after the email I sent 
 this morning. It is my pleasure to introduce you to Rui Pimenta and Layne H
 inton who are the organizers of Art Spin.\n\nAs mentioned\, Digifest has pa
 rtnered with Art Spin to host an event on the evening of May 9th called the
  Install Crawl. Crawl guests will be meeting at George Brown College's wate
 rfront campus (which is next to Corus Quay where the festival is happening)
  at 6:30\, to depart for the tour at 7. It will wrap up in Kensington Marke
 t around approx. 9 at a closing party for the festival.\n\nWithin current d
 rafts of the route there are three different stops in Kensington. In additi
 on to HackLab\, we are also working with SUMO Projects (223a Agusta)\, and 
 are exploring an outdoor projection.  Rui and Layne are in charge of choreo
 graphing the route\, they will have a more accurate sense of timing for the
  tour as we move closer to the event. \n\nWhen I visited HackLab a few Tues
 days ago we talked about the Install Crawl participants getting introduced 
 to HackLab through a brief tour of the space but more importantly encounter
 ing some of the great projects your membership are working on. You also men
 tioned that during Pedestrian Sunday's you sometimes spill out onto the str
 eet - that could also be an interesting thing to do as well. \n\nPlease exp
 ect to hear from Rui and Layne for some more details. And of course\, if yo
 u ever have any questions please feel free to be in touch with myself.\n\nI
  am thrilled that HackLab is a part of the tour!\n\nKindly\,\n\nSimon\n\n--
 \nSimon Rabyniuk
LAST-MODIFIED:20140408T204739Z
LOCATION:Hacklab.TO\, 170A Baldwin Street\, Toronto
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Art Spin / Digifest Install Crawl
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
