BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:HackLab.TO
DTSTART:20160229T000000Z
DTEND:20160229T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260512T040225Z
UID:s8gk2msfib0g91vblka0ncfh2c@google.com
CREATED:20160217T163652Z
DESCRIPTION:https://www.facebook.com/events/221678508175769/\n\nI went to C
 hina to find the places where everything gets made. This quest led me to fa
 ctories in suburbs of megacities\, towering electronics markets\, apartment
 s retrofitted as hackerspaces\, alleys full of tiny workshops\, and Hong Ko
 ng’s highest heights.\n\nI will share photos and stories of places I visite
 d and people I met\, along with some insights into the changing relationshi
 p to suppliers\, and changing global markets. I will focus on Shenzhen and 
 Yiwu\, two very different cities that are integral to global supply chains.
 \n\nThis research has been driven by a personal obsession with objects and 
 obsolescence.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20160228T232914Z
LOCATION:Hacklab\, 1266 Queen St W\, Toronto\, ON M6K 1L3\, Canada
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Sea of Commodities - Making in China Show and Tell
TRANSP:OPAQUE
