BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:HackLab.TO
DTSTART:20120428T170000Z
DTEND:20120428T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260512T040225Z
UID:g11afi2dbqgo75rhn1nmnauv0k@google.com
CREATED:20120424T201434Z
DESCRIPTION:Message Body:\nDear HackLab community\,\n\nI'm writing to you b
 ecause I am managing the programme for a visit to Toronto by one Jeremy Dav
 enport\, Deputy Director of the UK's Creative Industries Knowledge Transfer
  Network (CI-KTN). The CI-KTN (https://connect.innovateuk.org/web/creativek
 tn) aims to stimulate innovation in the creative industries\, and is very k
 een to learn and share examples of best practice with innovative Canadian c
 entres.\n\nWhile Mr. Davenport will be doing a bunch of official visits (OC
 AD\, MaRS etc.)\, he has expressed very strong interest in grassroots colle
 ctives\, the crowdsourcing of creative projects and learning about what's g
 oing on in the community-based centres in Toronto. I would very much like t
 o arrange for him to visit the HackLab\, if someone will be around to chat 
 while he's here.\n\nIdeally I'd like to take him to a Tuesday night beginne
 r session\, but he's only here from the 26th to the 28th of this month. Do 
 you know if there might be anything going on on the evenings of the 26th or
  27th\, or at any time on the 28th? Even if it's just a chat with some peop
 le from the collective\, I'm keen for him to learn more about how local hac
 kspaces operate here.\n\nAdditionally\, if you have any recommendations for
  digital/tech grassroots projects going on that might be of interest\, I'd 
 be happy to recommend them as well.\n\nWith regards\,\n\nJohn Preece\n\nSci
 ence and Innovation Officer\nBritish Consulate-General Toronto
LAST-MODIFIED:20221122T084258Z
LOCATION:Hacklab.to\, 170A Baldwin Street\, Toronto
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Visit by UK Creative Industries
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
