DESCRIPTION:**Eventbrite link TBA**\n\n**Eventbrite link TBA**\n\nArduino B
 eginners Workshop [parts extra]. For total beginners. All are welcome. $20 
 includes all fees + starter Arduino kit.\nA-Train and Zach will show you ho
 w to get started with Arduino\, the super-friendly microcontroller platform
  that even artists love. We’ll cover getting the software installed and goi
 ng\, hooking up the Arduino\, and a little bit of basic programming\, via e
 xplanation of the Examples. You too can cut and paste your way to a working
  project!\n***If you can't bring your own Arduino (any kind will do) and an
 y cables required to attach it to your laptop (typically an A to B USB cabl
 e)\, we'll be selling kits included with the price of admission. You'll als
 o need a laptop on which you can install software. You can purchase an Ardu
 ino at Creatron at  349 College St\, Toronto\, ON M5T 1S5 (or online\, of c
 ourse). The Arduino Uno is the recommended board for beginners\, but any ar
 duino will do if you have a more specialized project in mind.***\nFinding H
 acklab: We're at Queen and Dufferin\, NW corner\, buzz unit #12.
LAST-MODIFIED:20180607T234247Z
LOCATION:Hacklab\, 1266 Queen Street West #12\, Toronto\, ON\, Canada
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Arduino Beginners Workshop with ATrain & Zach
TRANSP:OPAQUE
