DTSTART:20151110T000000Z
DTEND:20151110T020000Z
DTSTAMP:20260512T040225Z
UID:es0nsgg667h6p4v7hjmi509emg@google.com
CREATED:20151022T140536Z
DESCRIPTION:In this workshop\, Rob and Alex demonstrate how to configure\, 
 flash\, and use the ESP-8266 Wifi module.  Learn how to do cool things with
  LUA and NodeMCU\, and check out some more complex things you can do with c
 ustom firmware.\n\nEasily connect your plant water sensor\, refrigerator\, 
 coffee machine\, shoes\, or cat to the internet\, thanks to the magic of th
 e Internet of Things!\n\nPlug-and-play USB-enabled ESP-8266 modules will be
  available at cost for $8 to the first 13 attendees (as that's how many we 
 have). \n\nRegister on EventBrite: http://www.eventbrite.com/e/building-the
 -internet-of-things-on-the-cheap-tickets-19207453009 
LAST-MODIFIED:20260405T052325Z
LOCATION:Hacklab\, 1266 Queen St W\, Toronto\, ON M6K 1L3\, Canada
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Building the Internet of Things on the cheap
TRANSP:OPAQUE
